{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the trie of the patterns with two more links per state: the failure link, to the state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the longest proper suffix of the state’s prefix that is also a prefix of some pattern, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the output link, to the nearest state along the failure links at which a pattern ends. A scan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the trie while the text matches and the failure links where it stops matching, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads each symbol of the text once and reports all the matches in O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for a text of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" symbols with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" matches.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","for match in automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\") {","    print(match.patternIndex, match.range)","}","\/\/ 1 1..<4   (\"she\")","\/\/ 0 2..<4   (\"he\")","\/\/ 3 2..<6   (\"hers\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matches come in order of where they end, and of those ending at one place, longest first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ranges count the text’s symbols from 0. The automaton is built once and is immutable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Symbols are mapped to dense indices at construction, through a 256-entry table when they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a dictionary otherwise, so a scan over bytes, such as a string’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", does no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hashing. When the states times the distinct symbols are few enough, every transition is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precomputed into a table, and a scan takes one load per symbol.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift#L29"},"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"nam